WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.440
- Do you have any?

00:00:01.440 --> 00:00:03.780
- [Host] Prince Harry's Memoir
"Spare" is the latest release

00:00:03.780 --> 00:00:06.330
from the Duke and Duchess
of Sussex's vast portfolio

00:00:06.330 --> 00:00:09.030
of shows, podcasts and books.

00:00:09.030 --> 00:00:10.590
After stepping down as working members

00:00:10.590 --> 00:00:12.780
of the British Royal family in 2020,

00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:14.610
no longer paid to represent the Crown,

00:00:14.610 --> 00:00:16.290
the couple have explored
new income streams

00:00:16.290 --> 00:00:19.200
as the next chapter of
their lives unfolds.

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:20.460
Here's what we do and don't know

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:22.950
about how Harry and
Meghan make their money.

00:00:22.950 --> 00:00:25.020
- [Reporter] Harry, are you
pressing money before family?

00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:26.864
Are you pressing money before family?

00:00:26.864 --> 00:00:28.611
(group chattering)

00:00:28.611 --> 00:00:31.630
- [Host] In "Spare", the
title and nod to having heir

00:00:32.538 --> 00:00:33.390
and a spare to the throne.

00:00:33.390 --> 00:00:35.340
Prince Harry speaks about topics ranging

00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:37.800
from physical altercations
with his brother William

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:40.650
to losing his virginity to
an older woman behind a pub.

00:00:40.650 --> 00:00:41.850
The couple signed a book deal

00:00:41.850 --> 00:00:43.860
with Penguin Random House widely reported

00:00:43.860 --> 00:00:45.750
to be worth $20 million

00:00:45.750 --> 00:00:48.000
which includes the
headline grabbing Memoir.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:50.820
- I called my publishers
rep right away and said,

00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:52.168
put me on the list.

00:00:52.168 --> 00:00:54.330
- The story is interesting
because it keeps evolving.

00:00:54.330 --> 00:00:58.290
- I'm sure it's partially
due to a lifestyle

00:00:58.290 --> 00:01:00.600
that they want and what can they sell?

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:03.090
- [Host] On the day of its
release, "Spare" was at the top

00:01:03.090 --> 00:01:06.420
of Amazon's best sellers
list alongside the book deal,

00:01:06.420 --> 00:01:08.820
there are multi-year agreements
with Netflix and Spotify

00:01:08.820 --> 00:01:11.493
reported to be worth roughly $120 million.

00:01:12.510 --> 00:01:14.700
Harry and Meghan will make
content for the two platforms

00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:17.310
through divisions of their
Art Trail organization.

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:18.780
Their first offering for Netflix,

00:01:18.780 --> 00:01:21.360
a six-part documentary series
had the streaming services

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:23.651
biggest debut for a documentary
titled by hours viewed

00:01:23.651 --> 00:01:25.650
the company said.

00:01:25.650 --> 00:01:27.270
- [Harry] We all have greatness within us.

00:01:27.270 --> 00:01:28.920
- [Host] Harry also has a
job at the Silicon Valley

00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:31.890
startup Better Up as Chief Impact Officer.

00:01:31.890 --> 00:01:33.660
His compensation package was not disclosed

00:01:33.660 --> 00:01:35.430
but jobs with that title
boast an average salary

00:01:35.430 --> 00:01:38.940
of $140,000 according to talent.com.

00:01:38.940 --> 00:01:40.734
The due conductors also
received an unknown

00:01:40.734 --> 00:01:42.960
but substantial sum from Harry's father,

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:44.970
according to a spokesperson,

00:01:44.970 --> 00:01:47.160
all together that would
total a lot more than the sum

00:01:47.160 --> 00:01:49.830
they received from then
Prince Charles in 2020.

00:01:49.830 --> 00:01:51.570
Financial releases from his estate reveal

00:01:51.570 --> 00:01:53.145
the Sussex's, along with William and Kate

00:01:53.145 --> 00:01:57.270
shared around $5.4 million
to fund their activities.

00:01:57.270 --> 00:01:59.250
Now, Harry and Meghan have security costs

00:01:59.250 --> 00:02:01.170
and living expenses to worry about.

00:02:01.170 --> 00:02:02.940
They live in Montecito, California

00:02:02.940 --> 00:02:05.850
where they bought a home
for over $14 million

00:02:05.850 --> 00:02:07.680
and there was the small task
of paying the Crown back

00:02:07.680 --> 00:02:10.590
the estimated 3 million it cost
to renovate Frogmore Cottage

00:02:10.590 --> 00:02:12.840
in Windsor, Harry and Meghan lived there

00:02:12.840 --> 00:02:15.796
after they were married,
until they moved to the US.

00:02:15.796 --> 00:02:18.120
Leaving the family business, so to speak,

00:02:18.120 --> 00:02:20.490
has opened up a world of new
opportunities for the couple

00:02:20.490 --> 00:02:22.770
but their sources of
revenue are less secure.

00:02:22.770 --> 00:02:24.870
At least King Charles III
has a guaranteed income

00:02:24.870 --> 00:02:27.420
from his property estates
and public funding.

00:02:27.420 --> 00:02:29.100
Representatives of the Duke Duchess

00:02:29.100 --> 00:02:31.800
didn't immediately respond
to a request for comment.

00:02:31.800 --> 00:02:33.990
It is possible Harry and
Meghan will need to continue

00:02:33.990 --> 00:02:36.670
making commercial deals to
sustain their lifestyle.

00:02:36.670 --> 00:02:39.337
(upbeat music)

